  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer array `nums` of length `n`.\n\nAn array is **trionic** if there exist indices `0 < p < q < n − 1` such that:\n\n* `nums[0...p]` is **strictly** increasing,\n* `nums[p...q]` is **strictly** decreasing,\n* `nums[q...n − 1]` is **strictly** increasing.\n\nOutput `true` if `nums` is trionic, otherwise output `false`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,3,5,4,2,6]\n\n**Output:** true\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nPick `p = 2`, `q = 4`:\n\n* `nums[0...2] = [1, 3, 5]` is strictly increasing (`1 < 3 < 5`).\n* `nums[2...4] = [5, 4, 2]` is strictly decreasing (`5 > 4 > 2`).\n* `nums[4...5] = [2, 6]` is strictly increasing (`2 < 6`).\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [2,1,3]\n\n**Output:** false\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThere is no way to pick `p` and `q` to form the required three segments.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `3 <= n <= 100`\n* `-1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
